At this point, I believe we may reasonably conclude the following:

1) The code takes *some* time to run
2) The code takes a disparate number of seconds to run depending on
who sent in the timings

> ggplot.times <- c(132.81, 31.629, 26.63, 162.974, 31.279,
+                   38.47, 29.683, 46.11, 39.745)
> chisq.test(x = ggplot.times, simulate.p.value = TRUE, B = 10^5)

data:  ggplot.times
X-squared = 344.3292, df = NA, p-value = 1e-05

2.a) We may cautiously posit this is due to different hardware and/or software
3) The users of ggplot2 have lots*** ofcombinations of CPUs, OSes,
RAM, R, and ggplot2

