Sorry, there were (at least) two mistakes in my previous email (corrected
version bellow);
	id begin in zero,
	emphasis on geom_path instead of geom_line.

Hi Felipe,

I guess you can use the id created by fortify to "merge" the result to the
original data.frame ("luck.mapDF"). This id would correspond to row number
in this data.frame (e.g. the number of each feature; you can use something

like luck.mapDF$id <- 0:(dim(luck.mapDF)[1] - 1)). After this, you can plot
the lines, but remember to set a "group" aesthetic for geom_path (for

instance id or group as resulting from fortify).

Hope this helps,
fernando

