You are unlikely to get usable data just looking at Intel clock speeds.  Memory access speeds can vary hugely between processor models that have similar clock speeds and depending on the mix of on-chip and off-chip processing, if for example the R code has poor locality of reference or the amount of memory access for data is large, then memory access speeds will be the dominant performance factor.  It would be useful to add in processor age and model to the data collected.

