Subject: scale-x issue
Message-ID: <3sdYB2cfrqQ.Le_q0RflkeEJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/3sdYB2cfrqQ/m/Le_q0RflkeEJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear all, seemingly a very simple issue, but I'm experiencing
difficulties in setting the x-axis values directly.
Here are some sample data to illustrate.

#Set the year span from 1999 to 2009
 >year=1999:2009
# assign the y-values
 >prop=c(.021,.027,.013,.014,.030,.060,.060,.103,.142,.118,.152)

# now plot
 >qplot(year,prop)

The x-axis is labelled every 2nd year starting at 2000. If I want to
ensure that every year is labelled I try the following:

 > qplot(year,prop, ylab="Proportion",
scale_x_continuous
(breaks=c(1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009)))

Again, the plot shows the x-axis unchanged - every 2nd year beginning
with "2000".
I'd appreciate a pointer to how I can ensure that all years are
labelled.

Many thanks,
Alan Kelly
Trinity College Dublin

From u5196f936ff792c35 at groups.google.com  Mon Sep  6 10:03:06 2010
From: u5196f936ff792c35 at groups.google.com (Brandon Hurr)
Date: Mon, 06 Sep 2010 10:03:06 +0000
Subject: Re: scale-x issue
Message-ID: <3sdYB2cfrqQ.PjXYiTY6mhIJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <3sdYB2cfrqQ.Le_q0RflkeEJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
References: <3sdYB2cfrqQ.Le_q0RflkeEJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
