Hi - I have tracks of elephant seals out in the North pacific that I'm
trying to plot base maps for. I've tried using borders() to provide
some spatial reference, but I'm having two problems. If I just use
coord_cartesian() one of the tracks ranges over 180 longitude, so the
lines jump and stretch all the way across the map. I also tried using
coord_map() with a mercator, so that I could set the limits (Hadley's
suggestion in an archived post), and while this projects the data, I'm
getting lots of horizontal lines across the image. lastly, if I try a
different projection, e.g. albers, or lambert, I get errors within
mapproj.

What I would like is a projected map with all the data - including the
one track that spans 180.

Following are the script with examples of each scenario, and my
session info.

Thanks,
Rob

