Thomas,

Thanks for giving a reproducible example and a sample image.

The following should give you an idea how to specify the title of the legend in this case as well as relabeling the colors themselves.

ggplot(data,aes(fill=fcolor_two,y=f1,x=x)) + geom_bar(position="dodge", stat="identity") +  scale_x_continuous(labels=c("100k","200k","b100k"),breaks=c(1,2,3)) + scale_fill_discrete(name='Title', labels=c('color 1', 'color 2'), breaks=c("#00a37c","#2dab00"))

I am confused by what you mean by, " All I want is a legend with only 2 entries and a different title." You only have two colors and no more in the legend.

As far as moving the legend... I'm not sure how to do that one.

Brandon

