Thomas,

Learn to use factors. That will make things much easier

library(ggplot2)
data <-
data.frame(Corpus=factor(c(1,2,1,2,1,2)),f1=c(70,75,80,84,90,95),x=facto
r(c(1,1,2,2,3,3), labels = c("100k", "200k", "b100k")))
ggplot(data,aes(fill=Corpus,y=f1,x=x)) +

		geom_bar(position="dodge", stat="identity")

Use scale to tweak the content of the legend

ggplot(data,aes(fill=Corpus,y=f1,x=x)) +

		geom_bar(position="dodge", stat="identity") +

		scale_fill_manual("Other title", value = c("purple",
"white"), labels = c("A", "B"), breaks = 1:2)

More examples at the ggplot2 website

Thierry

