Normally, you'd set the limits of the axis using the scale_*_** but it doesn't work because geom_bar() requires the y_min to be 0 (I think this is why it plots nothing).

ggplot(data,aes(fill=fcolor_two,y=f1,x=x)) + geom_bar(position="dodge", stat="identity") +  scale_x_continuous(labels=c("100k","200k","b100k"),breaks=c(1,2,3)) + scale_fill_discrete(name='Title', labels=c('color 1', 'color 2'), breaks=c("#00a37c","#2dab00")) + scale_y_continuous(limits=c(50,100))

You'll have to "zoom" in using coord_cartesian().

ggplot(data,aes(fill=fcolor_two,y=f1,x=x)) + geom_bar(position="dodge", stat="identity") +  scale_x_continuous(labels=c("100k","200k","b100k"),breaks=c(1,2,3)) + scale_fill_discrete(name='Title', labels=c('color 1', 'color 2'), breaks=c("#00a37c","#2dab00")) + coord_cartesian(ylim = c(50,100))

Mucks with the y axis breaks a bit.

Brandon

