Hi Everyone

Working with this on my actual data, I've run into a problem
that I didn't think of when I first posted the question;

df<-data.frame(path=1:5,a.1=rnorm(5), a.2=rnorm(5),bbnum.25=rnorm(5),
 dd.4.50=rnorm(5), eee.31.5=rnorm(5))

  path         a.1        a.2   bbnum.25     dd.4.50     eee.31.5
1    1  0.08595333  0.7309579 -0.4583091 -0.85701834  1.021900390
2    2 -0.54099131 -0.2382299  0.8426603  0.77227616 -0.259230826
3    3  0.45699980 -0.1509856  0.4171901 -0.84711629 -0.007809302
4    4 -0.65007115 -1.2413905  0.9613126 -0.14606821 -0.925703608
5    5 -1.93574364 -0.2711861  0.7053587 -0.07840072 -0.882576264

my problem is how to make this long.  i can't use
substr because the number of characters varies.  furthermore
for some, but not all, of the columns there's 2 times.  what
i'd like is:

path  t1  t2  variable  value
  1  1 NA a 0.08595333
  2  1 NA a -0.54099131
  3  1 NA a 0.45699980
  4  1 NA a -0.65007115
  5  1 NA a -1.93574364
  1  2 NA a  0.7309579
  2  2 NA a -0.2382299
  3  2 NA a -0.1509856
  4  2 NA a -1.2413905
  5  2 NA a -0.2711861
  1  25 NA bbnum -0.4583091
  2  25 NA bbnum  0.8426603
  3  25 NA bbnum  0.4171901
  4  25 NA bbnum  0.9613126
  5  25 NA bbnum  0.7053587
  1  4 50 dd -0.85701834
  2  4 50 dd  0.77227616
  3  4 50 dd -0.84711629
  4  4 50 dd -0.14606821
  5  4 50 dd -0.07840072
  1  31 5 eee   1.021900390
  2  31 5 eee  -0.259230826
  3  31 5 eee  -0.007809302
  4  31 5 eee  -0.925703608
  5  31 5 eee  -0.882576264

im pretty sure there's a solution involving strsplit, but
i've been working on it for a day and a half and i can't get
it...  strsplit is giving a list which i can't figure out
how to make into the data.frame.

any help would be greatly appreciated, and thanks so much
for the helpful replies so far!

best
-neal

