also i solved the problem in case anyone is interested.  as i
mentioned in my post and thierry noted again, the problem is to use
strsplit.  here's my solution:

df<-data.frame(path=1:5,a.1=rnorm(5), a.2=rnorm(5),bbnum.25=rnorm(5),
 dd.4.50=rnorm(5), eee.31.5=rnorm(5))

dfm<-melt(df,id="path")

f1<-function(vec) { vec[1] }
f2<-function(vec) { vec[2] }
f3<-function(vec) { vec[3] }

dfm$varname<-sapply(spvar,f1)
dfm$t1<-sapply(spvar,f2)
dfm$t2<-sapply(spvar,f3)

dfm
   path variable       value varname t1   t2
1     1      a.1 -0.05929815       a  1 <NA>
2     2      a.1 -2.13510854       a  1 <NA>
...
9     3 bbnum.25 -0.41941116   bbnum 25 <NA>
10    1  dd.4.50 -0.68719042      dd  4   50
...

thanks alot, i couldn't have done it without your help...  (hopefully
i wont be back!!!!)

