> > why it plots nothing).
> >
> > ggplot(data,aes(fill=fcolor_two,y=f1,x=x)) + geom_bar(position="dodge",
> > stat="identity") +
> >  scale_x_continuous(labels=c("100k","200k","b100k"),breaks=c(1,2,3)) +
> > scale_fill_discrete(name='Title', labels=c('color 1', 'color 2'),
> > breaks=c("#00a37c","#2dab00")) + scale_y_continuous(limits=c(50,100))
> >
> > You'll have to "zoom" in using coord_cartesian().
> >
> > ggplot(data,aes(fill=fcolor_two,y=f1,x=x)) + geom_bar(position="dodge",
> > stat="identity") +
> >  scale_x_continuous(labels=c("100k","200k","b100k"),breaks=c(1,2,3)) +
> > scale_fill_discrete(name='Title', labels=c('color 1', 'color 2'),
> > breaks=c("#00a37c","#2dab00")) + coord_cartesian(ylim = c(50,100))
> >
> > Mucks with the y axis breaks a bit.
