I'm awesome.

data <- data.frame(cluster = paste("Cluster", 1:4), size = c(0.5519, 0.2238, 0.1544, 0.0698), position = c(0.5519, 0.5519+0.2238, 0.5519+0.2238+0.1544, 0.5519+0.2238+0.1544+0.0698), position2 = c(0.3, 0.7, 0.85, 0.965))

ggplot(data, aes(x = factor(1), fill = cluster, weight=size)) +

geom_bar(width = 1) + geom_text(aes(x= 1.75, y=position2, label=size))+coord_polar(theta="y")+theme_bw() + opts(axis.title.x = theme_blank(), axis.title.y= theme_blank(), axis.text.x=theme_blank(), axis.text.y=theme_blank(), panel.grid.minor = theme_blank(), panel.grid.major = theme_blank(), panel.border = theme_blank(), axis.ticks=theme_blank())

/applause

I set the geom_text() with an x value of 1.75 and it puts it just outside of the circle. I also got rid of that random tick mark that was in the previous graph.

As far as the labels go. I think you could create a script of sorts that takes the percent of the pie or decimal of each section and places a position at 1/2 of the width. so... 0.55 / 2 = pos1... 0.55 + 0.22/2 = pos2... etc...

Brandon

