James,
I did the labels by hand in this case because I wasn't sure how to get
R to calculate what I wanted, quickly.

Something like this...

xy<-data.frame(x=c(60, 25, 15), y=c(0,0,0))

t<-length(xy[[1]]

xy$y<-1/2*xy$x

for (i in 2:length(xy[[1]])){
xy$y[i]<-xy$y[i]+xy$x[i-1]
}

I know that's probably a horrible example, but it is 'an' example.

Although, Josh has a good point.

Brandon

